    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="4454a05e-2a11-5ad4-8f76-f6a9b8cf6cc0" activityNameId="0d6dcce1-4908-5033-b11c-f2395ca1432e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Sewer system, construction, PP-HM pipe, SN 8, DN 300, profile 4</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Sewer system, construction, PP-HM pipe, SN 8, DN 300, profile 4
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: 9cfe82c7-6169-40ff-a7c7-4393bdc9154e
This process models 1 meter of installed sewer infrastructure PP-HM pipe and a trench depth of 3 meters. This process includes the production phase (A1–A3) and the construction phase/ transport (A4–A5) for 1 meter of installed PP-HM pipe, including trench excavation and backfilling. Disposal and deconstruction processes are excluded and modelled separately specific for each sewer system type. The operation of similar types of building machines across different processes is aggregated to one process.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: DN 300, profile 4, SN 8, according to SIA 190.Trench depth 3 meters. PP-HM pipe, ID 293 mm, outer diameter 315 mm, wall thickness 11 mm, 9.6 kg/m, 930 kg/m³. 
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_9cfe82c7-6169-40ff-a7c7-4393bdc9154e.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
